      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tomahawk%2C_Wisconsin"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Tomahawk traditionally traces its founding to the establishment of construction camps for a dam and the railroad in 1886.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tomahawk%2C_Wisconsin"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Founded primarily as a logging city in the 1890s, Tomahawk now has a diverse economy including Harley-Davidson and Northland Stainless.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.cityoftomahawkwi.com/general-info"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Washington Square Park in Tomahawk features a historic steam train named Old No. 19 that originally hauled timber.",
